zfsroot (2) blueberry-pie-os; urgency=medium

  * First boot zeroes the end of the partition it grows before it grows
    the pool, so the labels of a pool that once filled the card are not
    taken for the new pool's. A card that had run an earlier pool stopped
    responding at its first boot, and the next boot could not import its
    root. A partition that would grow too little for that end to be
    cleared is left as it is.
  * First boot tries again to grow the partition at the next boot when
    reading or writing the card failed.

 -- Maxwell <maxwell@blueberrypieos.com>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:22:28 +0000

